{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"Semiring","roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Semiring","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Semiring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Semirings\/Semiring.swift#L31"},"modules":[{"name":"Semirings"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Semiring","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:9Semirings8SemiringP"},"abstract":[{"text":"A semiring (S, ⊕, ⊗, 0̄, 1̄), the algebra of path problems (Mohri 2002; Gondran–Minoux 2008).","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","type":"inheritsFrom","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/SQ"]},{"title":"Inherited By","kind":"relationships","type":"inheritedBy","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/SelectiveSemiring"]},{"title":"Conforming Types","kind":"relationships","type":"conformingTypes","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/BooleanSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/BottleneckSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/CountingSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/LexicographicSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/MaxPlusSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/TropicalSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/ViterbiSemiring"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Semiring"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Equatable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SQ"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ extends a path by an edge and ⊕ combines alternative paths. The shortest-path entry points in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ShortestPaths answer a different question for each conformer. The tropical semiring gives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shortest paths, the bottleneck semiring widest paths, the Boolean semiring reachability, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counting semiring the number of paths."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A conformer implements the four requirements. The type system does not check the laws, and an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithm’s result is meaningful only when they hold:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊕ is associative and commutative, with identity "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ is associative, with identity "},{"code":"one","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":" annihilates: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a ⊗ 0̄ == 0̄ ⊗ a == 0̄"},{"type":"text","text":";"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ distributes over ⊕ from both sides."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"⊗ need not be commutative. Algorithms always compute "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distance ⊗ weight"},{"type":"text","text":", in path order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":" is not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdditiveArithmetic.zero"},{"type":"text","text":". No semiring type here is a number, and a tropical"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":" is +∞."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operators "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⊕"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⊗"},{"type":"text","text":" call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plus(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"times(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", so the two spellings always agree."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Prefer the methods where another module might declare the same operators, and inside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":". That macro folds an expression without these operators’ precedences, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(a ⊕ b == c)"},{"type":"text","text":" does not type-check, while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(a.plus(b) == c)"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/semirings\/semiring"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Operators","generated":true,"anchor":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/_(_:_:)-2ou28","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/_(_:_:)-93rtg"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/plus(_:)","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/times(_:)"]},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/one","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring\/zero"]}],"references":{"doc://Semirings/documentation/Semirings/BooleanSemiring":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifie